      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the comment isn\u0027t quite right for `vm_map_pages()`: `__vm_map_pages()` still bounds 4KB VMAs in kernel pages, with `vma_kernel_pages()` (aosp/4368056), and so does `iommu_dma_mmap_noncontiguous()` (aosp/4368058). So when `size` isn\u0027t a multiple of 16KB, a 4KB process would get a different limit depending on whether the IOMMU buffer is contiguous.\n\nThe existing kernel-page check also accepts every mapping that the byte check accepts, so skipping it for 4KB VMAs doesn\u0027t let anything new through. If the patch stays, would it be OK to keep this condition as it is, without the comment? The check in the entry points that I suggested on `dma_mmap_pfn()` would give both paths the same limit.",
